<blockquote class="uncited"><div>It so happens that my RT82 has a shift of reference frequency (at 144mHz -500Hz, at 70cm already more than 1kHz). When working in analog modes it is not a problem, but when using dmr (especially hotspot) it is already a problem. So far I solve the problem by introducing frequency correction on rt82. <br>In CPS the calibration tab is inactive.</div></blockquote>CPS calibration tab only reads and writes the data file for the STM32 based radios. <br>It only displays the data for the GD77 type radios , including RD5R <br><br><br>You can calibrate the frequency in the firmware<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Mar 07, 2024 6:16 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
