		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Reference frequency calibration on RT82]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3851&amp;p=29994#p29994"><![CDATA[
It so happens that my RT82 has a shift of reference frequency (at 144mHz -500Hz, at 70cm already more than 1kHz). When working in analog modes it is not a problem, but when using dmr (especially hotspot) it is already a problem. So far I solve the problem by introducing frequency correction on rt82. <br>In CPS the calibration tab is inactive.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=649">R9OBQ</a> — Thu Mar 07, 2024 3:14 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
